From: kc <kc@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run the rules that read only the PSI while kc analyzes

On kc, the session's collectDiagnostics has none of the compiler's
checkers to report: kc reports the errors it finds in the sources
itself. ValidateClasspath only waited for kc's analysis, on the main
thread, so it is left out (-Dkc.validateClasspath=true keeps it).

The rules run in two waves: the rules that read only the PSI on every
file, then those that read the Analysis API (RequiresAnalysisApi). The
first rule that reads kc's session waits for its analysis, so the first
wave runs while kc analyzes in the background. Each file's issues keep
the order of its rules, and the processors still see each file once.
With auto-correct, which changes the PSI, or -Dkc.waves=false, the
rules run in one wave.
